# An allowlist: the build context is the manifests, the toolchain pin and the Rust sources, and
# nothing else. `COPY . .` in `builder` hashes the whole context, so any file that reaches it is
# an input to the final `cargo build`. With `.github/`, the docs and the release-please files in
# the context, a commit that touched only a workflow or the changelog recompiled the workspace
# crates on every push. A new top-level directory the build needs has to be added here; leaving
# it out fails the build instead of silently compiling without it.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!src/
!apps/
!crates/

# Local build output inside the allowed directories.
**/target
**/*.rs.bk
